-- title:
--   Order of P(̃ j) at a point of the j-line is the root multiplicity
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field, let $a \in k$, and let $P \in k[X]$. Consider the level-one modular function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,1$, the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $k((q))$ over $k$ generated by the two series `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k 1`, where `jqModC k` is $q^{-1}$ times the reduction to $k$ of the power series $E_4^3\cdot\eta^{-24}$-type numerator `jNum` (so it is the $q$-expansion $\tilde j$ of the modular invariant), and let $\tilde j$ denote `jqModC k` viewed as an element of that field. Consider further the place $\mathrm{charLGeomPlaceOfPoint}\,k\,a$: the $k$-place of this field obtained by transporting, along the $k$-algebra isomorphism `ratFuncEquivCharLOneC` between $k(X)$ and $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,1$, the finite place of the rational function field attached to the irreducible polynomial $X - a$; here a place is a valuation subring containing $k$, proper and a principal ideal ring, and its `ord` of an element is minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation. The assertion is that the order of $P(\tilde j)$, the image of $P$ under evaluation at $\tilde j$, at this place equals $\operatorname{mult}_a(P)$, the multiplicity of $a$ as a root of $P$, regarded as an integer. For $P = 0$ both sides are $0$ by the conventions that $\mathrm{ord}\,0 = 0$ and that the root multiplicity of the zero polynomial is $0$.
--
--   This is the standard computation of the valuation of a polynomial expression in the uniformising coordinate at a rational point of the $j$-line, stated for the concrete level-one fibre field generated by $q$-expansions. It supplies the divisor-theoretic input used by the chart and covering computations on modular curves, among them [`ModularCurve.MultCovering.ord_nodeTgt_infChart_residue_of_digits`](thm.html#ModularCurve.MultCovering.ord_nodeTgt_infChart_residue_of_digits) and [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_componentCharts_annuli_isAttached_of_isModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_componentCharts_annuli_isAttached_of_isModel).
